{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true","id":1416109,"title":"Is this statement true?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-30T09:25:38-07:00","id":1416109,"title":"Is this statement true?","content":"So in the Mage the Ascension universe during the Dark Ages the sun revolved around the earth. Then during the Renaissance Copernicus (a Celestial Master) published his theories and the Consensus shifted and the solar system literally changed with it and now the earth revolves around the sun. (My teacher in high school irl told me that\u2019s where the word revolution comes from.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T09:37:12-07:00","id":1416113,"title":"","content":"Maybe in Mage first edition. But we've come a long way since then. <br /> <br /> Here's my take on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">the nature of the Consensus</a>. In a nutshell, reality is <i>influenced by</i> the Consensus, but it is not <i>the same as</i> the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:11:39-07:00","id":1416121,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> So what did happen when Copernicus published his theories? How did it change things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:13:38-07:00","id":1416122,"title":"","content":"It helped bring the Consensus in line with Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:16:00-07:00","id":1416123,"title":"","content":"Got it. Thanks. That\u2019s what I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:50:38-07:00","id":1416132,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, you're stuck with two options:<br /> <br /> 1) What Dataweaver said in the linked essay.<br /> <br /> 2) A collapsing set of different Earths that all coexisted and were slowly winnowed down to one.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that viewing the idea of geocentricism as the &quot;default&quot; is highly biased by the historical records. The first known person to apply skepticism and mathematics to the positioning of celestial bodies (instead of just trying to reinforce cultural assumptions) beat Copernicus to concluding a heliocentric model by ~1,700 years. However we know very little about him or his followers because they're only referenced by other people rather than being a full part of the historical record.<br /> <br /> We also had multiple competing models. Even if you were to assume geocentricism was &quot;true&quot; in the Dark Ages because most people believed it (though you could argue most people didn't actually care and we don't have records for a lot of people), which version of it? If only one version was &quot;true&quot; at the time, did the other planets revolve around the Earth, or did they revolve around the sun as it revolved around the Earth? After all, from a functional perspective even in modern physics the only reason to care about heliocentrism vs. geocentrism is how the sun and Earth relate to the rest of the objects in our solar system. If all that existed was the sun and the Earth, which revolved around which would be a semantic game as they'd be (and actually are) revolving around each other. But if you want to figure out where the sun, Venus, Earth, and Mars all are in respect to each other, recognizing the dominate force of the sun in a heliocentric model is vital.<br /> <br /> So to the question:<br /> <br /> At a minimum the statement is not universally true for Mage. Depending on how you view certain aspects of the setting it is either untrue, partially true, or it is both untrue and true in different versions of history.<br /> <br /> Also, revolution comes from Latin and the Latin root is as varied in use as the modern English word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T14:03:58-07:00","id":1416159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416132#post1416132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, you're stuck with two options:<br /> <br /> 1) What Dataweaver said in the linked essay.<br /> <br /> 2) A collapsing set of different Earths that all coexisted and were slowly winnowed down to one.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that viewing the idea of geocentricism as the &quot;default&quot; is highly biased by the historical records. The first known person to apply skepticism and mathematics to the positioning of celestial bodies (instead of just trying to reinforce cultural assumptions) beat Copernicus to concluding a heliocentric model by ~1,700 years. However we know very little about him or his followers because they're only referenced by other people rather than being a full part of the historical record.<br /> <br /> We also had multiple competing models. Even if you were to assume geocentricism was &quot;true&quot; in the Dark Ages because most people believed it (though you could argue most people didn't actually care and we don't have records for a lot of people), which version of it? If only one version was &quot;true&quot; at the time, did the other planets revolve around the Earth, or did they revolve around the sun as it revolved around the Earth? After all, from a functional perspective even in modern physics the only reason to care about heliocentrism vs. geocentrism is how the sun and Earth relate to the rest of the objects in our solar system. If all that existed was the sun and the Earth, which revolved around which would be a semantic game as they'd be (and actually are) revolving around each other. But if you want to figure out where the sun, Venus, Earth, and Mars all are in respect to each other, recognizing the dominate force of the sun in a heliocentric model is vital.<br /> <br /> So to the question:<br /> <br /> At a minimum the statement is not universally true for Mage. Depending on how you view certain aspects of the setting it is either untrue, partially true, or it is both untrue and true in different versions of history.<br /> <br /> Also, revolution comes from Latin and the Latin root is as varied in use as the modern English word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> When you say the first known person, do you mean Eratosthenes?<br /> <br /> Okay. My AP History teacher told us the modern use of the word revolution to mean change or upheaval came from Copernicus. (He went to Yale, but that doesn\u2019t necessarily mean he\u2019s right.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T14:41:17-07:00","id":1416165,"title":"","content":"Actually, I meant Aristarchus of Samos (a contemporary of Eratosthenes). One of the reasons Aristarchus generally gets forgotten besides the fact that almost nothing of his works remain, is that he couldn't demonstrate a core speculation: stellar parallax. While he correctly observed that the lack of stellar parallax to the human eye means that stars have to be extremely far away, they should still have some parallax for his model's assumptions to hold true; which requires telescopes to observe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:58:01-07:00","id":1416176,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I like learning stuff.<br /> <br /> Is stellar parallax relevant to the heliocentric theory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T16:21:19-07:00","id":1416178,"title":"","content":"Not really? At least not as long as we can launch things into space to see things directly.<br /> <br /> Stellar parallax is more important for disproving geocentric theories, or at least some of the assumptions behind them, of the time rather than directly proving heliocentric theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T19:00:49-07:00","id":1416195,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Was Aristarchus aware that the sun was a star?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T01:46:18-07:00","id":1416217,"title":"","content":"It's not really clear. Keep in mind that most of what we know of his work are things other people said about it.<br /> <br /> It seems like he assumed the sun and the stars were the same size, but that might have just been something to try to estimate how far away something that big would have to be to not have observable parallax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T04:03:29-07:00","id":1416224,"title":"","content":"Got it. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T06:19:24-07:00","id":1416243,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you play it to be honest. Later editions introduced ideas like the Earthly constants, yes. But I find that those... Cause more trouble than they add value.<br /> <br /> The whole setting is predicated on belief = reality. Take that away or water it down, and the setting stops making sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T06:30:08-07:00","id":1416247,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, saying that Consensus=Reality is what doesn't make sense; it gets you into dilemmas such as the best way to battle climate change in a belief=reality setting is to push climate change denial. <br /> <br /> The Consensus <i>has to</i> be wrong about some things, or the setting stops making sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T08:28:27-07:00","id":1416267,"title":"","content":"In the end, I think, it's one of those &quot;up to the storyteller&quot; things. If the storyteller likes a more poetic type universe, where belief is key, and therefore, the rules of the universe may have been very different before the Order of Reason and modern day, I think they could pull that off.<br /> <br /> I admit though, I prefer the idea of Earthly Constants too. Science doesn't develop in a vacuum. Someone, usually a number of people, has to make the observations, that lead to the calculations that lead to discovery. And most of these sorts of ideas: like the Earth being round, or the Earth not being the center of the universe are older than we think. A lot of the medieval belief that we talk about was strictly a European thing, and sometimes even THEY didn't completely believe what we think they believed.<br /> <br /> There's possibly a way to balance the concepts: Consensus is established by more than just one culture after all. Or by incorporating time elements into it: Consensus is defined not just by the people of the time, but people in the past and future. Or Consensus about particular observable phenomenon might be determined by other life forms as well. Animals likely wouldn't know or care about whether or not a human can cast a fireball, but they may be able to comprehend that the horizon has a curve to it, or that things fall when they're pushed off a table. That might be an explanation as to why gravity is an Earthly Constant, but the capabilities of mages could change so abruptly from the Mythic to the Modern age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:08:27-07:00","id":1416290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416267#post1416267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I think, it's one of those &amp;quot;up to the storyteller&amp;quot; things. If the storyteller likes a more poetic type universe, where belief is key, and therefore, the rules of the universe may have been very different before the Order of Reason and modern day, I think they could pull that off.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right. To clarify, my main objection was to the way the question about a purely subjective reality was being framed in terms of whether or not it <i>makes sense</i>. If you're going for whether or not it's \u201cpoetic\u201d, that's a whole different matter. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416267#post1416267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit though, I prefer the idea of Earthly Constants too. Science doesn't develop in a vacuum. Someone, usually a number of people, has to make the observations, that lead to the calculations that lead to discovery. And most of these sorts of ideas: like the Earth being round, or the Earth not being the center of the universe are older than we think. A lot of the medieval belief that we talk about was strictly a European thing, and sometimes even THEY didn't completely believe what we think they believed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In particular, one problem with the Consensus=Reality idea is that there's little reason why unintuitive notions would ever become reality. The belief that the Earth is round came about because of observations such as seeing ships sail past the horizon; but if the Consensus defines Reality and the Consensus was ever that the Earth is flat, then those observations would never take place. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416267#post1416267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's possibly a way to balance the concepts: Consensus is established by more than just one culture after all. Or by incorporating time elements into it: Consensus is defined not just by the people of the time, but people in the past and future. Or Consensus about particular observable phenomenon might be determined by other life forms as well. Animals likely wouldn't know or care about whether or not a human can cast a fireball, but they may be able to comprehend that the horizon has a curve to it, or that things fall when they're pushed off a table. That might be an explanation as to why gravity is an Earthly Constant, but the capabilities of mages could change so abruptly from the Mythic to the Modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually at the heart of the essay that I linked to at the start of this thread: there is no universal Consensus, because things like Correspondence Ranges, Gauntlet ratings, and separation in Time limit who can influence what. The asymmetric nature of time means that past beliefs influence the present far more than future ones do, and that present beliefs influence the future far more easily than they influence the past (this is what MRev called Historical Inertia); and the Gauntlet that isolates the Earth from the Umbra means that humans have little say about the nature of the Umbra; but also that any Willworking spirits that might reside in the other side of the Gauntlet have a greatly diminished influence on what Earth is like. <br /> <br /> But this rule of separation? <i>That's an objective rule about how the world works,</i> and isn't subject to the whims of the Consensus. More generally, there are object's rules about how belief influences reality; and those rules aren't subject to the Consensus. <i>Those</i> are examples of what MRev's Cosmological Constants and M20's Earthly Foundations are for: you literally cannot use the Consensus to change the rules of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:46:21-07:00","id":1416298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416290#post1416290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're absolutely right. To clarify, my main objection was to the way the question about a purely subjective reality was being framed in terms of whether or not it <i>makes sense</i>. If you're going for whether or not it's \u201cpoetic\u201d, that's a whole different matter. <br /> <br /> In particular, one problem with the Consensus=Reality idea is that there's little reason why unintuitive notions would ever become reality. The belief that the Earth is round came about because of observations such as seeing ships sail past the horizon; but if the Consensus defines Reality and the Consensus was ever that the Earth is flat, then those observations would never take place. <br /> <br /> <br /> That's actually at the heart of the essay that I linked to at the start of this thread: there is no universal Consensus, because things like Correspondence Ranges, Gauntlet ratings, and separation in Time limit who can influence what. The asymmetric nature of time means that past beliefs influence the present far more than future ones do, and that present beliefs influence the future far more easily than they influence the past (this is what MRev called Historical Inertia); and the Gauntlet that isolates the Earth from the Umbra means that humans have little say about the nature of the Umbra; but also that any Willworking spirits that might reside in the other side of the Gauntlet have a greatly diminished influence on what Earth is like. <br /> <br /> But this rule of separation? <i>That's an objective rule about how the world works,</i> and isn't subject to the whims of the Consensus. More generally, there are object's rules about how belief influences reality; and those rules aren't subject to the Consensus. <i>Those</i> are examples of what MRev's Cosmological Constants and M20's Earthly Foundations are for: you literally cannot use the Consensus to change the rules of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Earthly Foundations acting as a stabilizing force on the Consensus. I\u2019ll have to check that out in my copy of M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:10:10-07:00","id":1416326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416247#post1416247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, saying that Consensus=Reality is what doesn't make sense; it gets you into dilemmas such as the best way to battle climate change in a belief=reality setting is to push climate change denial. <br /> <br /> The Consensus <i>has to</i> be wrong about some things, or the setting stops making sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I don't see why that makes things not make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T14:46:27-07:00","id":1416353,"title":"","content":"It's right there in what you quoted. But let me try again.<br /> <br /> Your position is that we should have a Belief=Reality setup without any watering down such as the Earthly Foundations. But if we go with that, the only reason anything exists is because there is belief in it. That includes such things as climate change. So if you want to get rid of climate change, all you have to do is stamp out belief in climate change. Thus, climates change denial becomes the cure for climate change.<br /> <br /> You need <i>something</i> more nuanced than a simplistic \u201cBelief=Reality\u201d, or else you'll end up with cases such as this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T14:51:57-07:00","id":1416356,"title":"","content":"Well, the dominant Earthly Consensus is that magic isn't real.... so that's a big thing that doesn't make sense it if was true for the Reality of the setting as presented in a game where the players play characters that use magic.<br /> <br /> The most simple disproof of &quot;Consensus = Reality&quot; is rather simple: if Consensus is Reality, how did either come into existence? If they are the same thing, one can't be first. If Reality came first then it had rules before Consensus came into being. If Consensus came first, what gave it the form to create Reality at all (let alone the specific Reality that leads to the setting in Mage)?<br /> <br /> The Earthly Foundations are just codifying that Reality came first, and that the rules of Reality that even allow for Consensus to exist are immutable to Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T15:03:43-07:00","id":1416360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416353#post1416353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's right there in what you quoted. But let me try again.<br /> <br /> Your position is that we should have a Belief=Reality setup without any watering down such as the Earthly Foundations. But if we go with that, the only reason anything exists is because there is belief in it. That includes such things as climate change. So if you want to get rid of climate change, all you have to do is stamp out belief in climate change. Thus, climates change denial becomes the cure for climate change.<br /> <br /> You need <i>something</i> more nuanced than a simplistic \u201cBelief=Reality\u201d, or else you'll end up with cases such as this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that doesn't make it not make sense. That makes it not track to reality, which we're talking about a fictional world in which clap your hands if you believe actually causes magic to happen.<br /> <br /> The issue is your confusing science in game with how science works in real life.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a scientist like you would be in real life, the Sons of Ether are the only ones who really do that. And there's a reason why their science is weird.<br /> <br /> Science is a tool, used by the Technocracy. All that stuff about Observation and reporting what you see is propaganda. Meant to brainwash sleepers into just believing what they observe, while the Technocrats have an unseen thumb on the scale all the while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:08:18-07:00","id":1416374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416360#post1416360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that doesn't make it not make sense. That makes it not track to reality, which we're talking about a fictional world in which clap your hands if you believe actually causes magic to happen.<br /> <br /> The issue is your confusing science in game with how science works in real life.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a scientist like you would be in real life, the Sons of Ether are the only ones who really do that. And there's a reason why their science is weird.<br /> <br /> Science is a tool, used by the Technocracy. All that stuff about Observation and reporting what you see is propaganda. Meant to brainwash sleepers into just believing what they observe, while the Technocrats have an unseen thumb on the scale all the while.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if that's the case, then it's the Technocracy's actions that don't make sense. What possible gain could they achieve by deciding that the Earth should be round rather than flat? \u201cThings are the way they are because the Technocracy wants them to be\u201d only makes sense if there's something in it for the Technocracy. And there's a long list of things in science that either wouldn't be worth the effort to make it so or are directly counter to the Technocracy's goals. <br /> <br /> And no, I'm not confusing science in game with how science world in real life. I haven't been talking about science at all. I've been talking about how <i>Magick</i> works in game. There are rules to it, rules that cannot be changed by the Consensus or by mages. <i>That</i>, not science, is what I'm referring to when I say that there's a Reality independent of the Consensus. That, and things like the existence of the Gauntlet and the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:38:09-07:00","id":1416377,"title":"","content":"The real problem there it's not so much a logical inconsistency as an ethical one.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy supposed goal it's to protect humanity, and they are it's resposible for science current state AND the best way to solve a problem it's to pretend it doesn't exist - then Technocracy has to explain why they insist on discovering new dangerous things like meteorites, climate change, new sicknesses...etc.<br /> <br /> I mean, we come from a state of human belief where God/The Divine literally had our back (well, at least the back of &quot;good&quot; people). Whereas now it's said earth could be vaporized by a cosmic gamma ray at any minute w/o science being able to do anything about it (at least as far as public science made it known). I can understand wizards being salty about their godly overseers, but one can't talk of a world ruled by humanity when we're &quot;motes of cosmic dust&quot;.<br /> <br /> But maybe the goal of the Technocracy was never to help humanity, but just to rule over it? So they keep on inventing problems like climate change and sicknesses to keep the masses under control. Meanwhile the heroic Traditions ally with anti-vaxeers and such to end sicknesses for good...Not an aesop I would want my game to deliver, mind you, but not something inherently contradictory...<br /> <br /> ...except that the Technocracy isn't supposed to be <i><b>that </b></i>evil since 1e. There's no way in hell 2e+ Technocracy (depicted as mostly trully idealistic, if a bit misguided, people) would condone generating dangers to humanity that are above and beyond what dragons never were ... Hence the ethical lack of coherence on their part, if this is true. <hr /><br /> Not that there aren't <i>logical </i>and <i>methaphisical </i>inconsistencies aplenty in &quot;Consensus = Reality&quot; position. They easily appear if one starts to examine how this world ruled by the Consensus <i>came to be</i>. As <i>Heavy Arms</i> it's pointing out.<br /> <br /> If things so fundamental as gravity or the morphology of the cosmos depend on human belief: What was there before humans existed?, was there <i>nothing </i>before humans? Then how did humans <i>came to be</i> if human belief it's necessary for there to be <i>time</i> (and thus<i> succesion of events</i>) in the fist place?<br /> <br /> Being has to, at least, exist simultaneously to belief (one would usually say that it predates belief). But these <i>&quot;beliefs&quot; that create a universe simultaneously with the believer</i> are... something of a wonder. These are nothing like &quot;I believe science works&quot;. One can imagine a world of wonder where gravity it's caused by frost giants below the earth, but one can't easily imagine a world without things like geometry or physics. <i>How did these beliefs formed?</i> I can't really imagine how to even <i>describe </i>such &quot;&quot;&quot;beliefs&quot;&quot;&quot; w/o ending on something that would be Foundational in all but name<br /> <br /> Even then Avatars, Prime, the Consensus itself...aren't things that people believe in. Magick should by all means collapse into itself unless, again, the Consensus includes somewhere a set of &quot;beliefs&quot; that look nothing like what we (AND Mage) usually understands as a belief.<br /> <br /> I have explored some of the complexities and posibilities of a purely consensual reality in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon\">another thread</a>: Disclaimer: That thread it's about head-canons, I'm not claiming anything of that crazyness it's canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-01-2020, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:40:58-07:00","id":1416378,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Reality is more than the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:54:14-07:00","id":1416380,"title":"","content":"In some fairness to the Technocracy, they're dealing with inheriting things the Order of Reason did that they wouldn't currently agree with, and they would argue a lot of things that come about from their efforts that are contrary to their ideals are just manifestations of Paradox. Though that gets into a question of why Reality had Paradox to deal with (getting into metaphysical issues instead of logical ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T19:23:23-07:00","id":1416402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416374#post1416374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that's the case, then it's the Technocracy's actions that don't make sense. What possible gain could they achieve by deciding that the Earth should be round rather than flat? \u201cThings are the way they are because the Technocracy wants them to be\u201d only makes sense if there's something in it for the Technocracy. And there's a long list of things in science that either wouldn't be worth the effort to make it so or are directly counter to the Technocracy's goals.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not confusing science in game with how science world in real life. I haven't been talking about science at all. I've been talking about how <i>Magick</i> works in game. There are rules to it, rules that cannot be changed by the Consensus or by mages. <i>That</i>, not science, is what I'm referring to when I say that there's a Reality independent of the Consensus. That, and things like the existence of the Gauntlet and the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, firstly because a round earth more or less has a set surface area. You're not going to get anymore 'discovering a whole new continent' with a sailing ship anymore. Instead you need a rocket ship. Something well out of the public's grasp to build. So instead of crossing into the Umbra by sailing the ocean blue, now you launch into the void above. Why? Because it's imperative to the Technocrats that Crossing the Umbra be difficult. Not impossible, but difficult.<br /> <br /> No, you've been talking about Climate Change. There could be all kinds of reasons why climate change is a thing. Because a big part of the game is that while the Technocrats are the masters, the pioneers of engineering consensus, they're not alone anymore. The Traditions fight back and put things of their own in the consensus and that's why Magic still exists at all. Maybe Climate Change exists because a bunch of Verbena convinced people it does. Maybe climate change exists because the Technocracy is trying to phase out fossil fuels entirely, and needs an excuse while also putting into the consensus the ideas needed for Terraforming. Maybe climate change exists as part of a Technephandi plot. Or maybe it was just incompetence, with two departments of the Technocracy pushing out ideas and sleepers put the two ideas together in unexpected ways. It wouldn't be the first time, given nukes were invented that way. Sleepers taking two principles that the Technocracy had pushed into the consensus and putting them together into something unexpected and dangeous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T09:41:31-07:00","id":1416487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416402#post1416402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, firstly because a round earth more or less has a set surface area. You're not going to get anymore 'discovering a whole new continent' with a sailing ship anymore. Instead you need a rocket ship. Something well out of the public's grasp to build. So instead of crossing into the Umbra by sailing the ocean blue, now you launch into the void above. Why? Because it's imperative to the Technocrats that Crossing the Umbra be difficult. Not impossible, but difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that statement to be untrue, for both historical reasons and logical ones<br /> <br /> HISTORY: Columbus believed his round earth would allow to travel to the Indias. It turns out there was a pretty big continent he hadn't anticipated in this sphere: America.<br /> <br /> THEORY: There's such thing as calculating the area of a flat surface. A flat earth *can* <i>easily </i>have a set surface area: Just see Terry Pratchett's <i>discworld</i>. Or flat-earthers, who believe there's an impenetrable giant wall of ice blocking the edge of the world (so water doesn't fall).<br /> <br /> As far as I can see, the only thing a round earth does better it's to avoid people dying by &quot;falling&quot; of the edge. Considering how hard it's to get there anyway, it doesn't seem like it would deserve much attention, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-02-2020, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T09:42:34-07:00","id":1416488,"title":"","content":"My point about climate change wasn't about how it came to be. It was about how best to combat it. In a Consensus=Reality setup, the best way to combat it is to deny it. More generally, this applies to <i>any</i> problem that confronts you: convince the Consensus to deny it, and the problem goes away. <br /> <br /> Which, as others have pointed out, is logically consistent \u2014 or would be, of the various groups in-setting actually favored that approach. But there's a general assumption in the setting that the proper way to address these issues is that denial is a bad thing \u2014 that the first thing to do when dealing with a problem is to raise awareness of it. Exactly the opposite of what the Consensus=Reality model suggests. Thus, the model doesn't make sense. <br /> <br /> And then there are all of the other inconsistencies that have been pointed out, such as things existing that the Consensus doesn't acknowledge. <br /> <br /> I'll agree that there's a certain thematic purity to the Belief=Reality position, of which Consensus=Reality is a large part. And I'm not saying that it's wrong to play the game that way; it's your game, play it however you want. But that doesn't mean that it makes sense, or that acknowledging objective elements of the setting that marr that purity <i>doesn't</i> make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T04:44:24-07:00","id":1416607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416402#post1416402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you've been talking about Climate Change. There could be all kinds of reasons why climate change is a thing. Because a big part of the game is that while the Technocrats are the masters, the pioneers of engineering consensus, they're not alone anymore. The Traditions fight back and put things of their own in the consensus and that's why Magic still exists at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this kinda ignores the biggest factor in influencing the Consensus ... the Sleepers. There's a reason every magical group that tries to control the Consensus does so <i>indirectly</i>, by trying to influence the beliefs of the Sleepers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T14:32:55-07:00","id":1416641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416247#post1416247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Consensus <i>has to</i> be wrong about some things, or the setting stops making sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But it doesn't make sense. Never has. It would ruin the game for me if it did. It is Magick. Magick isn't real, and nay supernatural based game by definition cannot and should not adhere to making sense&quot; more than is necessary for a functional game. The very mechanics with these crazy dice pools, the don't make sense. They create an illusions of sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T16:20:55-07:00","id":1416654,"title":"","content":"It's your choice<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't really have a strong stance about the limits of the Consensus since, at least, 2e version of the Mythic Threads. From that point and onwards one can harbor doubts about the reach of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> It has been said that &quot;it creates more problems than it's worth&quot;... but I have yet to hear one. Conversely I much preffer to think that the Consensus it's a reality warping force that competes with other forces. And one that has a few limits that are hard to bypass (and not w/o consequences). Because:<br /> <br /> *It's much more easy to imagine a world where we didn't create things like time and space. Mage itself doesn't go so far: The Tradition's Lore states that the universe was created by the One and the Pure Ones (that latter became the Avatars). You have powers beyond the Consensus rigth there.<br /> <br /> *It's better for Crossover, because it allows to explain how other supers aren't affected by Paradox in ways that are more compatible with their own Lore.<br /> <br /> *Humanity becomes capable of doing some minor stuff on their own, by playing within the rules. The Hubris of mages believing to be the sole resposible for the development of the Human race can now be explored.<br /> <br /> *If not everything comes from human experience, <i>the universe can harbor mysteries</i>. I find very ironical that someone agianst &quot;magick making sense in fictional worlds&quot; would defend that the mtaphisics of the Council of Nine have to be rigth ALL the time. Things outside the Consensus imply, for mages, that &quot;there are things out there undreamth by your philosophy&quot;. I like the freedom to say mages might, perhaps, not have everything figured out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T06:33:45-07:00","id":1416716,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that a &quot;Traditions are 100% right&quot; view of the setting is kind of deprotagonising for the other two playable factions ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T07:50:12-07:00","id":1416727,"title":"","content":"From my opinion the whole Consensus is not automatically reality could easily explained with that every sleeper is a proto mage that has the power to controll reality but the pure ones like Jahwe or Gaia set rules that the mages can not defy unless they are choosen by a pure one. This would explain why vampires and Garou would not stop to exist despite the consensus stopped believing in them but things like dragons need to hide or go into umbra because the former are beings that where made by pure ones and so to delate them from universe you need to get on the power lvl of a pure one or do the hard work of killing all of them. The latter are just spirits that need to act like the consensus unless they where powered by a supernatural being. Angels and so Fallen are just the high lvl spirits directly created or empowered by Jahwe while the triad is the archangelequivalent for gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:38:07-07:00","id":1416991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416109-is-this-statement-true?p=1416716#post1416716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that a &amp;quot;Traditions are 100% right&amp;quot; view of the setting is kind of deprotagonising for the other two playable factions ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how Consensus being everything really makes the Traditions any more right than the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Like, this whole thread is full of stances on things that are just... Not bad if that makes sense, but so odd as to be kind of bewildering. Like if you were to be walking down a hallway and an old friend just stepped through the wall. It's not unpleasant, but weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:39:08-07:00","id":1417070,"title":"","content":"I think its easier to assume that 'Consensus' could be shaped by more than one factor. Maybe human perception/belief dominates such limits insofar as human (and mage) activity is concerned but that doesn't mean there can't be other influences. <br /> <br /> I tend to think of there being a single, largely immutable (by mortals at least) framework with plenty of stuff within that frame that is mutable according to human-derived consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T20:35:55-07:00","id":1417246,"title":"","content":"I think part of it might be a terminology issue: the way I'd phrase it would be something like\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cI think its easier to assume that \u2018Reality\u2019 could be shaped by more than one factor. Maybe human perception/belief (i.e., \u2018Consensus\u2019) dominates such limits insofar as human (and mage) activity is concerned but that doesn't mean there can't be other influences.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}